{
  "what": "Score records of the detector core on small cases. Every expected score was worked BY HAND from the definition in model/detector.py's docstring, and the sums are written out in each case's 'worked' lines. Nothing here was produced by the model.",
  "definition": "y_k[i] = sum over the channels c the filter reads and j = 0..T-1 of w[k][c][j] * x_c[i-(T-1)+j], samples before the stream taken as zero; r = y (rectifier 0, pass) or |y| (rectifier 1, abs); z_k[i] = sum of the last P values of r_k; a[i] = sum over k of h[k] * z_k[i]; score[i] = floor(a[i] / 2^shift).",
  "format": "config.filters is a list of filters; a filter maps a channel number (a string here, since this is JSON) to that channel's row of coefficients, OLDEST SAMPLE FIRST. frames[i] is frame i, one value per channel. records[i] is the score record expected for frame i.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "s16x1-pulse-in-order",
      "why": "The tap order. Coefficients (1, 2, 3) are the pulse (1, 2, 3) in order; the pulse's first sample is at j = 1, so the peak is at j + T - 1 = 3. Coefficients reversed would give 3*1 + 2*2 + 1*3 = 10 at i = 3; a filter one sample late would give 8 there.",
      "profile": "s16x1",
      "config": {"filters": [{"0": [1, 2, 3]}], "head": [1], "rectifier": 0, "pool": 1, "score_shift": 0},
      "frames": [[0], [1], [2], [3], [0], [0]],
      "worked": [
        "score[i] = 1*x[i-2] + 2*x[i-1] + 3*x[i]",
        "i=0: 1*0 + 2*0 + 3*0 = 0",
        "i=1: 1*0 + 2*0 + 3*1 = 3",
        "i=2: 1*0 + 2*1 + 3*2 = 8",
        "i=3: 1*1 + 2*2 + 3*3 = 14",
        "i=4: 1*2 + 2*3 + 3*0 = 8",
        "i=5: 1*3 + 2*0 + 3*0 = 3"
      ],
      "records": [
        {"index": 0, "epoch": 0, "flags": 0, "score": 0},
        {"index": 1, "epoch": 0, "flags": 0, "score": 3},
        {"index": 2, "epoch": 0, "flags": 0, "score": 8},
        {"index": 3, "epoch": 0, "flags": 0, "score": 14},
        {"index": 4, "epoch": 0, "flags": 0, "score": 8},
        {"index": 5, "epoch": 0, "flags": 0, "score": 3}
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "s16x1-impulse",
